## C ABI

`rust/capi` builds `lib{{ module }}_capi`, a C ABI over the Rust crate with the
generated header `rust/capi/include/{{ module }}.h` and a hand-written C++ wrapper
`{{ module }}.hpp` beside it. Wheels ship the library under `{{ module }}/lib` and
both headers under `{{ module }}/include/{{ module }}`, and the Python extension
links against it rather than compiling the crate in. The tests compile a C and a
C++ program against the installed package to prove the wheel is consumable. Other
projects build against the installed wheel with `{{ module }}.get_include()`,
`get_library_dirs()`, `get_libraries()`, and `get_prefix()`.

`HATCH_RS_LIBRARY_SOURCE` chooses where the library comes from at build time:
`bundled` (the default, for wheels), `external` (a prebuilt library found
through `HATCH_RS_LIBRARY_ROOT`, pkg-config, or the conda prefix), or `direct`
(compile the crate in).
